    <tags>pptx powerpoint diff compare presentation slides review cli foss cross-platform</tags>
    <summary>A diff tool to compare two PowerPoint decks -- completely local, no cloud upload.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
pptxdiff is a single-file, client-side tool for comparing two PowerPoint decks (or many pairs at
once), rendered with real fidelity and diffed on text, formatting, images, tables, charts,
animations, transitions, speaker notes, and more -- with a full reviewer workflow (approvals,
comments, history) built in. Nothing is ever uploaded anywhere; parsing, rendering, and diffing
all run locally in your own browser.

This package installs the [pptxdiff npm CLI](https://www.npmjs.com/package/pptxdiff) globally via
`npm install --global pptxdiff`, the same command documented in the project's own README as
"Option B -- npm (global install)". It requires Node.js (>= 18), pulled in automatically as a
Chocolatey dependency on the `nodejs` package.

## Usage

After installing, run:

    pptxdiff

This starts a small local static-file server on an OS-assigned free port and opens the app in
your default browser. There is no separate server/daemon left running afterward beyond that one
process, and no data ever leaves your machine.

## Features

- High-fidelity `.pptx` rendering plus deep diffing: text (word-level highlighting), fonts,
  color, alignment, position, borders, hyperlinks, images, charts, tables, backgrounds,
  animations, transitions, speaker notes, embedded fonts, and slide master/layout inheritance.
- Deck-level comparison (not just 1:1 pairs) -- added / removed / moved / changed / identical
  slide detection, plus duplicate-slide detection.
- A full reviewer workflow: multiple reviewers, per-slide and per-diff approve/reject, threaded
  comments, and an approval history log.
- Batch mode for comparing many deck pairs at once.
- A three-way merge planner plus a real (beta) merged `.pptx` export.
- Exports to PDF, standalone HTML, JSON, CSV, Markdown, Notion, Confluence, and more.
- Fully offline-capable -- every runtime dependency (React, JSZip, the rendering library, fonts)
  is vendored, not loaded from a CDN.

See the project README (https://github.com/sugatoray/pptxdiff) and documentation site
(https://sugatoray.github.io/pptxdiff/) for the full feature list.
]]></description>
